#sortorder:2
#showas:背叛的希望
A very difficult scenario. An increased number of factions, and it's set to difficulty 7.
This difficulty is good for someone who is skilled at AI War 2.

This is on the "linked rings" map type, with 110 planets. Ghost AI type, which heavily uses cloaking forces.
Your starting fleet is set to "Classic," which has the most basic available options.

Every faction here is allied to the AI, with the exception of the Dark Spire who still hate everyone:

The Nanocaust is a mechanical plague, spreading from planet to planet infecting ships which it will then send back at you.

Marauders, human pirates that will occasionally appear and try to attack you, with the goal of capturing the planet to use as a base to strengthen themselves.

Macrophages, which are giant space bug Harvesters that destroy ships for metal, and return it to their homes, creating new Harvesters and spreading to other planets.

The Devourer Golem is a bit different. It's always there, and does not expand in any way. Instead it roams the galaxy, looking for ships to eat. It's essentially undefeatable, so best stay away.

The Dark Spire have Vengeance Generators on a few planets, which absorb energy from units that die there, and uses it to warp in ships to cause havoc; if left unchecked, it can create new Generators, and be a very large problem.